"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[471],{921(e,o,t){t.r(o),t.d(o,{_pageData:()=>s,default:()=>a});var n=t(641);const s=JSON.parse('{"path":"/bagisto-connector/troubleshooting-faq.html","title":"Troubleshooting & FAQ","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"prev":"/bagisto-connector/logs-and-history.md"},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"bagisto-connector/troubleshooting-faq.md"}'),r={name:"troubleshooting-faq.md"},a=(0,t(6262).A)(r,[["render",function(e,o,t,s,r,a){return(0,n.uX)(),(0,n.CE)("div",null,[...o[0]||(o[0]=[(0,n.Fv)('<h1 id="troubleshooting-faq" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#troubleshooting-faq"><span>Troubleshooting &amp; FAQ</span></a></h1><p>If you encounter issues while configuring or using the WooCommerce to Bagisto Connector, consult this guide for common solutions.</p><hr><h2 id="frequently-asked-questions" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#frequently-asked-questions"><span>Frequently Asked Questions</span></a></h2><h3 id="_1-the-connection-test-fails-what-should-i-do" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-the-connection-test-fails-what-should-i-do"><span>1. The connection test fails. What should I do?</span></a></h3><p>Verify the following:</p><ul><li>Ensure your Bagisto Site URL is correct and does not have a trailing slash.</li><li>Ensure the API Token is valid, active, and has the necessary permissions in Bagisto.</li><li>Check if your server firewall or security plugins are blocking outbound cURL requests.</li></ul><h3 id="_2-products-are-not-syncing-during-bulk-sync-why" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-products-are-not-syncing-during-bulk-sync-why"><span>2. Products are not syncing during Bulk Sync. Why?</span></a></h3><p>Bulk Sync relies on WordPress background cron jobs.</p><ul><li>Ensure that <code>WP_CRON</code> is functioning correctly on your server.</li><li>Verify that you have synced <strong>Categories</strong> and <strong>Attributes</strong> before attempting to sync Products.</li></ul><h3 id="_3-orders-are-failing-to-sync" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-orders-are-failing-to-sync"><span>3. Orders are failing to sync.</span></a></h3><p>Orders require the associated products and customers to exist in Bagisto first. If a product in the order hasn&#39;t been synced, the order sync will fail. Sync your Customers and Products first.</p><h3 id="_4-how-do-i-stop-an-ongoing-bulk-sync" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-how-do-i-stop-an-ongoing-bulk-sync"><span>4. How do I stop an ongoing Bulk Sync?</span></a></h3><p>The bulk sync runs in the background. While there isn&#39;t a direct &quot;stop&quot; button, you can manage the queue using a WP Cron manager plugin, or clear the queue directly from the database if absolutely necessary.</p><hr><h2 id="common-error-log-messages" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#common-error-log-messages"><span>Common Error Log Messages</span></a></h2><ul><li><strong>&quot;Not connected with Bagisto. Please create connection...&quot;</strong><ul><li><em>Solution:</em> You haven&#39;t successfully saved your connection settings. Go to the Connection tab and authenticate.</li></ul></li><li><strong>&quot;No user roles created in the Bagisto...&quot;</strong><ul><li><em>Solution:</em> You must create at least one user role/customer group in your Bagisto admin panel and assign it as the default in the plugin&#39;s Settings.</li></ul></li><li><strong>&quot;Search string can not be empty.&quot;</strong><ul><li><em>Solution:</em> When using the specific ID exclusion or inclusion filters, ensure you are formatting the input correctly.</li></ul></li></ul><hr><h2 id="support" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#support"><span>Support</span></a></h2><p>If you need further technical assistance, custom feature development, or have questions not covered in this documentation, please reach out to our support team.</p><ul><li><strong>Support Ticket:</strong> <a href="https://webkul.uvdesk.com/en/customer/create-ticket/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Create a Ticket at Webkul UVDesk</a></li><li><strong>Email:</strong> support@webkul.com</li></ul><p>When contacting support, please provide your <strong>Log</strong> details and screenshots of your <strong>Settings</strong> to help us resolve your issue faster.</p>',22)])])}]])}}]);